{"title":"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_CanadaMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution CanadaMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Andrea and Lauren are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> kilometers apart. They bike toward one another with Andrea traveling three times as fast as Lauren, and the distance between them decreasing at a rate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> kilometer per minute. After <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes, Andrea stops biking because of a flat tire and waits for Lauren. After how many minutes from the time they started to bike does Lauren reach Andrea?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/a/08a462b11071b9d29e5236254bd18c9c20b349d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 20 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B)}\\ 30 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C)}\\ 55 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D)}\\ 65 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E)}\\ 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let their speeds in kilometers per hour be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/d/10db40cc18d7471c355651971b33d25580f36e42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/d/28d2763dd690247d2ef2c6a39da93856949dbd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/8/7d8399082f4b025a539c9fc5da1e07750c97851a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_A=3v_L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"15\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/8/a28db62a8252c016b21e8f52cc2ea02f0efcbbd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_A+v_L=60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"17\" />. (The second equation follows from the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/a/87a7a619f7e42c9dd20c55cf338d69d507745413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\mathrm km/min = 60\\mathrm km/h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"163\" height=\"18\" />.) This solves to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/c/f7ca96e853175591123da0971db5c692dc32c9ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_A=45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79ec6573e9623729e6e5423328a6b3a4dffa9138.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_L=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>As the distance decreases at a rate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> kilometer per minute, after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes the distance between them will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/d/17d78ae2f05f140c2c69a76ab90d1bf5d1116205.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20-5=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /> kilometers.\n</p><p>From this point on, only Lauren will be riding her bike. As there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> kilometers remaining and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79ec6573e9623729e6e5423328a6b3a4dffa9138.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_L=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, she will need exactly an hour to get to Andrea. Therefore the total time in minutes is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/3/49356d877b021d55f7da9f6118dc8d49504e10c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+60 = \\boxed{65}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because the speed of Andrea is 3 times as fast as Lauren and the distance between them is decreasing at a rate of 1 kilometer per minute, Andrea's speed is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919c6a9c0b084df1dfde15943ec5c5897af9f039.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4} \\textbf{km/min}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"38\" />, and Lauren's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/e/62e95639ca6424f8bcba4c98a8b27d04879b1644.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} \\textbf{km/min}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"37\" />. Therefore, after 5 minutes, Andrea will have biked <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/8/808c9445adbe9db44ee675902e6296f23f125591.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4} \\cdot 5 = \\frac{15}{4}km$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"107\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>In all, Lauren will have to bike <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df6a83e3fe5f325cfd7d18e781342d60248804c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20 - \\frac{15}{4} = \\frac{80}{4} - \\frac{15}{4} = \\frac{65}{4}km$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"225\" height=\"38\" />. Because her speed is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/e/62e95639ca6424f8bcba4c98a8b27d04879b1644.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4} \\textbf{km/min}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"37\" />, the time elapsed will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/4/8d4d382cfcbd9d135284df592c2bd2d58992618e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{65}{4}}{\\frac{1}{4}} = \\boxed{\\textbf{D) 65}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"104\" height=\"47\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the distance between them decreases at a rate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> kilometer per minute when they are both biking, their combined speed is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> kilometer per minute. Andrea travels three times as fast as Lauren, so they travel at speeds of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" /> kilometers per minute and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> kilometers per minute, respectively. \n</p><p>After <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes, the distance between them will have decreased by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> kilometers, so they will be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/a/45a68cf2ed22ee191d4f5d3f7af67c1c39838556.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20-5 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> kilometers apart when Andrea stops. Then, Lauren will take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/f/fbfc4368eb265a5495830ee17b931a1f62edfb67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{15}{\\frac{1}{4}} = 15*4=60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"135\" height=\"45\" /> more minutes to reach Andrea. \n</p><p>They started to bike <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> minutes before Andrea stopped, so the total time Lauren passed from the time they started biking to the time Lauren reached Andrea is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52bc8cc218ebf03800ce091928e7b1ed5917c4bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60+5=65$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> minutes. Hence, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/a/71acce36806eb6af8d70ca16cebaedf84d31fd53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 65}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />. ~azc1027\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YJigRBg0LIQ\">https://youtu.be/YJigRBg0LIQ</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_CanadaMath\">Video Solution CanadaMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution CanadaMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/qu6hXScTKUI?si=anISa0NjZR3bIJeS&amp;t=1402\">https://youtu.be/qu6hXScTKUI?si=anISa0NjZR3bIJeS&amp;t=1402</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A\">2009 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">Problem 19</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016233311\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.049 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.065 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 277/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6352/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.618      1 -total\n 56.92%    8.320      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 41.69%    6.095      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7821:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016233311 and revision id 264616. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}